      },
      "message": "fix(import): give the STEP face evaluation cap measured headroom; a finer pass over a continuous face keeps the coarser mesh\n\n#1546's per-face evaluation cap (25 M) refused healthy models: 10208.STEP\nat the 60 M facet budget was refused on face #1073, which converges at\n28.07 M evaluations, and 32050.STEP used 92 % of the cap at the default\nbudget.\n\n- FACE_EVAL_CAP is 150 M: 5.3x the heaviest healthy face measured, and a\n  runaway face still ends in 10-15 s in release.\n- A refinement pass that trips the cap on a face proven continuous\n  (step_continuity: analytic, or a B-spline/NURBS with interior knot\n  multiplicity <= degree, finite points and positive weights, divided\n  only inside its own parameter range) keeps the coarser mesh at its own\n  chord, as a pass over the facet budget does. Any other trip still\n  refuses by name; the #1536 smear (and sc_logo.step's face #836, whose\n  division range ran to u = -2e51) still refuse.\n- A continuous face refused on its first pass is no longer called\n  discontinuous.\n- step_guard's tests move to step_guard_tests.rs (400-line law).\n\nFixes #1568\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
