      "message": "fix(import): a STEP pass is continuous only if every tripped face is; the out-of-range flag outlives the pass\n\nReview fixes for PR #1578:\n- Guarded::tripped() no longer reports only the first face that ran out:\n  the pass counts as continuous only if every tripped face is proven and\n  in range, and the refusal names the first one that is not.\n- Meter::reset() keeps the out-of-range flag, so a fallback never keeps\n  a coarser pass that divided the face outside its parameter range.\n- NURBS weights below 1e-9 of the net's largest are not proven.\n- Kept carries eval_capped; the reduced-fidelity log line names the\n  evaluation cap instead of memory when that is why refinement stopped.\n- Pins for the range clause (a rational patch divided over u from\n  -2e51), the sticky flag, two faces tripping in one pass, NURBS x/y/z,\n  w and knot finiteness, within's finiteness, swept surfaces, the weight\n  floor and eval_capped; each mutation-checked.\n\nFixes #1568\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
